id: pm-jjqyzd
title: "The two-call agent cold start proposed as canonical costs more tokens than the four-call protocol it replaces, and no gate measures either"
description: "Measured on the live workspace, contracts --summary plus next costs 5,028 tokens while the operating rules' context, search, list-open and list-in-progress sequence costs 4,647 and returns strictly more workspace state. The orientation path is the most repeated read sequence in the product and no measurement governs which protocol is documented as canonical."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:docs",measurement,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-07T11:17:30.747Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T15:20:19.908Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T15:13:31.843Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T15:13:31.843Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A fixed orientation corpus exists and reports token cost per documented protocol, including the composed alternatives, on a stable workspace snapshot; The canonical orientation protocol is selected from that measurement and the number is recorded on the item that documents it; Orientation cost is a case in the tokens-per-completed-task replay gate rather than a separate mechanism, and a regression fails CI; Docs, agent guidance blocks, and generated plugin templates all name the measured winner, and a conformance check fails when they disagree"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Documented orientation is the cheapest protocol that answers the orientation question, chosen by measurement and defended by a gate"
value: The most frequently executed read sequence in the product stops being selected on call count and starts being selected on the resource agents actually spend
why_now: "An open chore is about to document the more expensive protocol as canonical in docs and plugin templates, which would propagate the regression to every generated agent surface"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: Replaced prose-selected cold start with a measured capability-equivalent replay selector and regression gate
expected_result: "The orientation protocol named canonical is the one with the lowest measured token cost for the state it returns, the measurement is recorded, and a regression fails a gate"
actual_result: "The fixed 101-item completed-task replay measures context --for orient at 1,055 estimated tokens, the historical four-read sequence at 2,293, and contracts --summary plus next at 4,798. The gate selects context intent and fails if configured canonical work is not the measured winner."
