  "2026-08-31T13:24:39.475Z","harness:codex","Measurement evidence: the existing tokens-per-completed-task corpus now contains three capability-equivalent orientation protocols on independently seeded 101-item workspaces. Results: context --for orient = 1,055 tokens; historical context/search/open/in-progress sequence = 2,293; contracts --summary + next = 4,798. The gate fails on protocol capability drift, a non-winning canonical id, corpus drift, or token ceiling regression."
  "2026-08-31T15:13:29.898Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: linked replay-gate suite passed 11 tests. Fixed 101-item workspaces measure capability-equivalent orientation protocols at 1,055 tokens for context --for orient, 2,293 for the historical four-read sequence, and 4,798 for contracts plus next. The exact 100% repository coverage gate, typecheck, static-quality assurance, token-accounting gates, and docs/skills verification passed. The six-operation transport floor also passed with 20 iterations; the default three-sample local run was host-load-sensitive, so the higher-sample result is the governing local performance evidence and CI remains the clean-host merge gate."
